Z||000000||fiero56||03-03-2000||11:37 AM||||Figured somebody would have beat me to this one.<P>I just got the latest issue of AW yesterday. Says, GM isn't going to be bringing the Opel(Fiero) over. Too bad! From the picture that car is sweet. Would be the best car GM has or probably will ever have(maybe next to the Corvette). Somebody made a really big mistake at GM.<P>Look at the latest "Impalla". What a piece of crap. They're scared to go against the grain. Just imagine how many of those Opel speedsters would sell here. And for how much $$$. ||||reg||8
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||03-03-2000||04:54 PM||||as always, no flames please..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I saw a civic del sol from the back, and it looked somewhat like a modern notchback fiero (what it could have evolved into I mean).. looked pretty cool actually, with a 2.8 in the back, it might not be a bad little car. (unfortunately the civic has a little engine in the front.)<P>might be interesting to make a body kit for the fiero that was similar in style to the del sol. Most of the fiero body kits (total conversions) seem to have the fastback style, some even have a functional hatchback like the Finale. I think a notchback body kit would be cool.<P>anyway, getting back on topic.. what's the new Opel look like?||||reg||1
