Z||000012||Patrick's Dad||03-05-2000||08:30 PM||||This is what happens when bean counters run a company....<P>This is a very nice looking ride. I'd like to see it brought over to do battle with the Miata, the S2000, and the new MR2....<P>GM also has an Opel, the one that the Catera is based on, with the LS-1 under the hood. They project that they'd only sell 1,000 V-8 Cateras (The only RWD in the Caddy line, until the Evoq comes), so we're (America) chopped liver.... Oh, well, Gerneral, I guess there's the Lincoln LS-8 (Not for me, but GM should still be watching FoMoCo).<P>I also agree with the comment about the Impaler (Spelling error intended). Like so many others, including our beloved, GM gets it right, just in time to discontinue it.||||reg||9
Z||000013||DJRice||03-06-2000||09:42 AM||||I was hoping that GM would want to re-inspire my interest in their products with that new Monte Carlo, but its rear end is all wrong.  Completely goofy looking.  I do, however, enjoy the commercials with Taz.<P>The viper was the the last car out of America that has Cajones and Character.  But that new T-bird hasnt hit the street yet!||||reg||1
