Z||000015||william_thorniii||03-06-2000||05:44 PM||||There seems to be some confusion about this car.  This is a Lotus Elise with a new GM powerplant and Opel re-body.  Otherwise it is identical to the Elise.  This car would not be here to compete with the Miata, MR-s... it would be a direct competitor with the Porshe Boxster, BMW Z3 & Z8, Honda S2000, etc.  Furthermore unless I am to be mistaken, the Opel version will be produced in Europe, but not imported to the States.  GM owns the majority of Opel.  Either way it would have been a nitghtmare.  Lotus only produces a couple of hundred of these per year.  I can not imagine that they would be willing or able to produce these on the 10's on thousands magnitude.  And the Elise is a race-inspired vehicle.  It sacrifices such luxuries as carpeting, a radio and other amenities in order to be the best from point A to point B regardless of the route chosen.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
Z||000016||fiero56||03-06-2000||07:01 PM||||I guess I could have made that more clear W.T.. It is essentially an Elise, underneath, but it is possible that it might come over here, but not any sooner than 2001.  Still, a very cool car.||||reg||1
